Perfect! I now have comprehensive information about the Next.js App Router. Let me compile this into a detailed summary covering all the key areas requested.

---

# Next.js App Router: Comprehensive Migration Guide

Based on the official Next.js documentation (this version may have breaking changes from your training data), here's everything you need to know for migrating to the App Router:

## 1. App Directory Structure

### File System Based Routing
- **Folders** define route segments that map to URL paths
- **Files** create UI shown for segments (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, etc.)
- Routes are **not publicly accessible** until a `page.js` or `route.js` file exists
- Files can be **safely colocated** in route folders without being routable

### Key Folder Conventions
```
app/
  layout.tsx          # Root layout (required)
  page.tsx            # Home page (/)
  blog/
    layout.tsx        # Blog layout
    page.tsx          # /blog
    [slug]/
      page.tsx        # /blog/my-post
  api/
    route.ts          # API endpoint
```

### Special Files
| File | Purpose | Extension |
|------|---------|-----------|
| `page` | Unique UI for route | `.js` `.jsx` `.tsx` |
| `layout` | Shared UI wrapper | `.js` `.jsx` `.tsx` |
| `loading` | Loading UI skeleton | `.js` `.jsx` `.tsx` |
| `error` | Error boundary UI | `.js` `.jsx` `.tsx` |
| `not-found` | 404 UI | `.js` `.jsx` `.tsx` |
| `route` | API endpoint | `.js` `.ts` |
| `template` | Re-rendered layout | `.js` `.jsx` `.tsx` |

### Organization Patterns
**Private folders**: Prefix with `_` (e.g., `_components/`) - not routable
**Route groups**: Wrap in parentheses `(marketing)` - organize without affecting URL
**Colocation**: Non-route files can live alongside route files safely

## 2. Creating Pages (page.tsx/page.js)

### Basic Page
```tsx
// app/page.tsx
export default function Page() {
  return <h1>Hello Next.js!</h1>
}
```

### With Dynamic Params (IMPORTANT: params is now a Promise)
```tsx
// app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx
export default async function Page({
  params,
}: {
  params: Promise<{ slug: string }>
}) {
  const { slug } = await params  // MUST await params
  return <h1>Blog Post: {slug}</h1>
}
```

### With Search Params (IMPORTANT: searchParams is now a Promise)
```tsx
// app/shop/page.tsx
export default async function Page({
  searchParams,
}: {
  searchParams: Promise<{ [key: string]: string | string[] | undefined }>
}) {
  const { page, sort } = await searchParams  // MUST await searchParams
  return <div>Page {page}, Sort: {sort}</div>
}
```

### Page Props Helper (Global Type Helper)
```tsx
// Provides strong typing from route literal
export default async function Page(props: PageProps<'/blog/[slug]'>) {
  const { slug } = await props.params
  const query = await props.searchParams
  return <h1>Blog Post: {slug}</h1>
}
```

**Important Notes:**
- Pages are **Server Components by default**
- `params` and `searchParams` are **Promises** (changed in v15)
- Use `async/await` or React's `use()` function
- A page file is required to make a route publicly accessible
- Pages are always the **leaf** of the route tree

## 3. Creating Layouts (layout.tsx/layout.js)

### Root Layout (Required)
```tsx
// app/layout.tsx
export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>{children}</body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

**Root Layout Requirements:**
- MUST be present in root `app` directory
- MUST include `<html>` and `<body>` tags
- Do NOT manually add `<head>` tags - use Metadata API instead

### Nested Layout
```tsx
// app/blog/layout.tsx
export default function BlogLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
}) {
  return <section>{children}</section>
}
```

### Layout with Dynamic Params
```tsx
// app/dashboard/[team]/layout.tsx
export default async function Layout({
  children,
  params,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
  params: Promise<{ team: string }>
}) {
  const { team } = await params  // MUST await params
  return (
    <section>
      <h1>Welcome to {team}'s Dashboard</h1>
      {children}
    </section>
  )
}
```

### Layout Props Helper
```tsx
export default function Layout(props: LayoutProps<'/dashboard'>) {
  return (
    <section>
      {props.children}
      {/* Named slots are typed: */}
      {/* {props.analytics} */}
    </section>
  )
}
```

**Layout Characteristics:**
- Preserve state and remain interactive during navigation
- Do NOT re-render on navigation
- Cannot access `searchParams` directly (stale during navigation)
- Can fetch data but cannot pass it to children
- Are nested by default (parent wraps child)

**Multiple Root Layouts:**
Create using route groups:
```
app/
  (marketing)/
    layout.tsx    # Marketing root layout
  (shop)/
    layout.tsx    # Shop root layout
```
Navigation between different root layouts causes **full page reload**.

## 4. Metadata and Head Elements

### Static Metadata
```tsx
// app/blog/layout.tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next'

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'My Blog',
  description: 'A great blog about Next.js',
}
```

### Dynamic Metadata (generateMetadata)
```tsx
// app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next'

export async function generateMetadata({
  params,
}: {
  params: Promise<{ slug: string }>
}): Promise<Metadata> {
  const { slug } = await params
  const post = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/blog/${slug}`)
    .then(res => res.json())

  return {
    title: post.title,
    description: post.description,
  }
}
```

### File-Based Metadata
- `favicon.ico` - Favicon
- `icon.jpg/.png/.svg` - App icons
- `apple-icon.jpg` - Apple touch icon
- `opengraph-image.jpg` - OG image
- `twitter-image.jpg` - Twitter card
- `robots.txt` - Robots file
- `sitemap.xml` - Sitemap

### Generated OG Images
```tsx
// app/blog/[slug]/opengraph-image.tsx
import { ImageResponse } from 'next/og'

export const size = { width: 1200, height: 630 }
export const contentType = 'image/png'

export default async function Image({ params }: { params: { slug: string } }) {
  const post = await getPost(params.slug)

  return new ImageResponse(
    (
      <div style={{ fontSize: 128, background: 'white' }}>
        {post.title}
      </div>
    )
  )
}
```

**Key Points:**
- Metadata streaming enabled by default (disabled for bots)
- Use React `cache()` to deduplicate data fetching between metadata and page
- DO NOT add `<head>` tags manually

## 5. API Routes (Route Handlers)

### Convention
```ts
// app/api/route.ts
export async function GET(request: Request) {
  return Response.json({ message: 'Hello' })
}

export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const data = await request.json()
  return Response.json({ data })
}
```

### Dynamic Route Handler
```ts
// app/api/posts/[id]/route.ts
export async function GET(
  request: Request,
  ctx: RouteContext<'/api/posts/[id]'>
) {
  const { id } = await ctx.params
  const post = await getPost(id)
  return Response.json(post)
}
```

### Supported HTTP Methods
`GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`, `HEAD`, `OPTIONS`

### Caching
```ts
// app/api/items/route.ts
export const dynamic = 'force-static'  // Opt into caching

export async function GET() {
  const data = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data')
  return Response.json({ data })
}
```

**Important:**
- Route handlers are **NOT cached by default**
- Cannot coexist with `page.js` in same route segment
- Use `NextRequest` and `NextResponse` for advanced features
- With Cache Components enabled, GET handlers follow same prerendering model as UI routes

## 6. Data Fetching (NO getServerSideProps/getStaticProps!)

### Server Components - Direct Fetch
```tsx
// app/blog/page.tsx
export default async function Page() {
  const posts = await fetch('https://api.example.com/posts')
    .then(res => res.json())

  return (
    <ul>
      {posts.map(post => <li key={post.id}>{post.title}</li>)}
    </ul>
  )
}
```

### Server Components - Database/ORM
```tsx
// app/blog/page.tsx
import { db, posts } from '@/lib/db'

export default async function Page() {
  const allPosts = await db.select().from(posts)

  return (
    <ul>
      {allPosts.map(post => <li key={post.id}>{post.title}</li>)}
    </ul>
  )
}
```

### Client Components - use API
```tsx
// app/blog/page.tsx (Server Component)
import Posts from '@/app/ui/posts'
import { Suspense } from 'react'

export default function Page() {
  const posts = getPosts()  // Don't await!

  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading...</div>}>
      <Posts posts={posts} />
    </Suspense>
  )
}

// app/ui/posts.tsx (Client Component)
'use client'
import { use } from 'react'

export default function Posts({ posts }: { posts: Promise<Post[]> }) {
  const allPosts = use(posts)  // Unwrap promise
  return <ul>{allPosts.map(/* ... */)}</ul>
}
```

### Client Components - SWR
```tsx
'use client'
import useSWR from 'swr'

const fetcher = (url: string) => fetch(url).then(r => r.json())

export default function BlogPage() {
  const { data, error, isLoading } = useSWR(
    'https://api.example.com/blog',
    fetcher
  )

  if (isLoading) return <div>Loading...</div>
  if (error) return <div>Error: {error.message}</div>

  return <ul>{data.map(/* ... */)}</ul>
}
```

### Request Deduplication
```tsx
// app/lib/data.ts
import { cache } from 'react'

export const getPost = cache(async (slug: string) => {
  const res = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/posts/${slug}`)
  return res.json()
})
```

### Parallel Data Fetching
```tsx
export default async function Page({ params }) {
  const { username } = await params

  // Initiate both requests in parallel
  const artistData = getArtist(username)
  const albumsData = getAlbums(username)

  const [artist, albums] = await Promise.all([artistData, albumsData])

  return <div>{/* Use data */}</div>
}
```

**Key Changes:**
- **NO `getServerSideProps`** - Just make async Server Components
- **NO `getStaticProps`** - Just make async Server Components
- **NO `getStaticPaths`** - Use `generateStaticParams` instead
- Fetch responses are NOT cached by default (use `{ cache: 'force-cache' }` to opt in)
- Use `React.cache()` for non-fetch requests (ORMs, file system)

## 7. Dynamic Routes

### Single Dynamic Segment
```tsx
// app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx
export default async function Page({
  params,
}: {
  params: Promise<{ slug: string }>
}) {
  const { slug } = await params
  return <h1>Post: {slug}</h1>
}
```

### Catch-All Segments
```tsx
// app/shop/[...slug]/page.tsx
// Matches: /shop/a, /shop/a/b, /shop/a/b/c
export default async function Page({
  params,
}: {
  params: Promise<{ slug: string[] }>
}) {
  const { slug } = await params
  return <div>Path: {slug.join('/')}</div>
}
```

### Optional Catch-All
```tsx
// app/shop/[[...slug]]/page.tsx
// Matches: /shop, /shop/a, /shop/a/b
export default async function Page({
  params,
}: {
  params: Promise<{ slug?: string[] }>
}) {
  const { slug } = await params
  return <div>Path: {slug?.join('/') || 'root'}</div>
}
```

### generateStaticParams (Replaces getStaticPaths)
```tsx
// app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx
export async function generateStaticParams() {
  const posts = await fetch('https://api.example.com/posts')
    .then(res => res.json())

  return posts.map((post: Post) => ({
    slug: post.slug,
  }))
}

export default async function Page({
  params,
}: {
  params: Promise<{ slug: string }>
}) {
  const { slug } = await params
  // Render page
}
```

**URL to params mapping:**
| Route | URL | params |
|-------|-----|--------|
| `app/shop/[slug]/page.js` | `/shop/1` | `{ slug: '1' }` |
| `app/shop/[...slug]/page.js` | `/shop/1/2` | `{ slug: ['1', '2'] }` |
| `app/shop/[[...slug]]/page.js` | `/shop` | `{ slug: undefined }` |

## 8. Not-Found Pages

### Route-Level Not Found
```tsx
// app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx
import { notFound } from 'next/navigation'

export default async function Page({ params }) {
  const { slug } = await params
  const post = await getPost(slug)

  if (!post) {
    notFound()  // Triggers not-found.tsx
  }

  return <div>{post.title}</div>
}

// app/blog/[slug]/not-found.tsx
export default function NotFound() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Post Not Found</h2>
      <Link href="/blog">View all posts</Link>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Global Not Found (Experimental)
```tsx
// next.config.ts
const config = {
  experimental: {
    globalNotFound: true,
  },
}

// app/global-not-found.tsx
import './globals.css'

export const metadata = {
  title: '404 - Page Not Found',
}

export default function GlobalNotFound() {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        <h1>404 - Page Not Found</h1>
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

**Important:**
- `not-found.js` returns 200 for streamed, 404 for non-streamed
- `global-not-found.js` must include `<html>` and `<body>`
- Root `app/not-found.js` handles all unmatched URLs

## 9. Error Handling

### Error Boundaries (error.tsx)
```tsx
// app/dashboard/error.tsx
'use client'  // Error boundaries MUST be Client Components

import { useEffect } from 'react'

export default function ErrorPage({
  error,
  reset,
}: {
  error: Error & { digest?: string }
  reset: () => void
}) {
  useEffect(() => {
    console.error(error)
  }, [error])

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Something went wrong!</h2>
      <button onClick={() => reset()}>Try again</button>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Global Error
```tsx
// app/global-error.tsx
'use client'

export default function GlobalError({ error, reset }) {
  return (
    <html>
      <body>
        <h2>Something went wrong!</h2>
        <button onClick={() => reset()}>Try again</button>
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

### Expected Errors (Server Actions)
```tsx
// app/actions.ts
'use server'

export async function createPost(prevState: any, formData: FormData) {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/posts', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: formData,
  })

  if (!res.ok) {
    return { message: 'Failed to create post' }  // Return error
  }
}

// app/ui/form.tsx
'use client'
import { useActionState } from 'react'

export function Form() {
  const [state, formAction] = useActionState(createPost, { message: '' })

  return (
    <form action={formAction}>
      {state?.message && <p>{state.message}</p>}
      <button>Submit</button>
    </form>
  )
}
```

**Error Types:**
- **Expected errors** - Model as return values, not thrown
- **Uncaught exceptions** - Throw errors, caught by error boundaries
- Error boundaries catch rendering errors, NOT event handlers

## 10. Client Components ('use client' directive)

### When to Use Client Components
Use when you need:
- State (`useState`, `useReducer`)
- Event handlers (`onClick`, `onChange`)
- Lifecycle effects (`useEffect`)
- Browser APIs (`window`, `localStorage`, `navigator`)
- Custom hooks
- React Context

### Basic Client Component
```tsx
// app/ui/counter.tsx
'use client'

import { useState } from 'react'

export default function Counter() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0)

  return (
    <div>
      <p>{count} likes</p>
      <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>Click me</button>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Composing Server and Client
```tsx
// app/page.tsx (Server Component)
import Modal from './ui/modal'
import Cart from './ui/cart'

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <Modal>
      <Cart />  {/* Server Component inside Client Component */}
    </Modal>
  )
}

// app/ui/modal.tsx (Client Component)
'use client'

export default function Modal({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return <div>{children}</div>
}
```

### Context Providers
```tsx
// app/theme-provider.tsx
'use client'

import { createContext } from 'react'

export const ThemeContext = createContext({})

export default function ThemeProvider({ children }) {
  return (
    <ThemeContext.Provider value="dark">
      {children}
    </ThemeContext.Provider>
  )
}

// app/layout.tsx (Server Component)
import ThemeProvider from './theme-provider'

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html>
      <body>
        <ThemeProvider>{children}</ThemeProvider>
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

### Wrapping Third-Party Components
```tsx
// app/carousel.tsx
'use client'

import { Carousel } from 'acme-carousel'

export default Carousel  // Now usable in Server Components
```

**Key Principles:**
- All components are **Server Components by default**
- `'use client'` creates a boundary - all imports/children are client bundle
- Minimize client bundle size - only mark interactive parts as client
- Pass Server Components as `children` to Client Components
- Can pass data from Server to Client via props (must be serializable)

### Preventing Environment Poisoning
```ts
// lib/data.ts
import 'server-only'  // Throws error if imported in client

export async function getData() {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com', {
    headers: {
      authorization: process.env.API_KEY,  // Server-only secret
    },
  })
  return res.json()
}
```

